Title: VAULT FOURTEEN
Author: Daniel Crowe
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. WAREHOUSE LOFT - NIGHT

Marcus briefs the crew. Museum floor plan projected on brick.
MARCUS
We don't touch the diamond. We take the sketch behind it.

INT. VAN - NIGHT

Gear check. CANVAS TUBE, replica painting, maintenance vests.

EXT. MUSEUM - NIGHT

Rain. Sloane watches guard patterns from a parked car.
SLOANE
Someone already made us. They know we're coming tonight.

INT. SERVICE CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Pak kills the keypad. Camera loop live.
PAK
Twelve-second holes. Don't blink.

INT. CLOSED GALLERY - NIGHT

Laser grid. Reese mirrors a path with chalk on the floor.

INT. VAULT ANTEROOM - NIGHT

Decoy lifted. Vermeer study revealed. Swap begins.
MARCUS
Replica in. Original out. Twenty-second holes — move.

INT. MUSEUM LOBBY - NIGHT

Maintenance disguise. Guard nods them through.

EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Van pulls away clean. No alarms.

INT. VAN - MOVING - NIGHT

Sloane's phone — unknown number: THEY KNOW.
SLOANE
We had no digital footprint. Who's texting?

INT. WAREHOUSE LOFT - NIGHT

Sketch unrolled under lights — a Rembrandt, unmistakable. Marcus finds a micro-dot on the frame — museum inventory sticker, fresh.
MARCUS
We weren't stealing art. We were delivering it. Question is to who.

FADE OUT.


THE END
